        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T22:15:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Cable support for Revision is optional, so we could put it in but I don\u0027t know how many cables will actually report it",
      "parentUuid": "21fdbc5e_d16f9793",
      "revId": "d9f970db98d333cc8e6bdacbbb4160daa0fec9c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "636c3de1_1de2500a",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 230,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T01:19:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently there are not any features dependent on a cable\u0027s USB PD minor revision, so I\u0027m not currently planning to add it. But it\u0027s definitively something to think about.\n\nIf we start enabling features which depend on a cable at least defining fields added in the USB PD 3.1 spec (like USB4 v2 asymmetric mode), then I think we\u0027ll need to add Get_Revision for SOP\u0027. As Diana mentioned currently it is optional, but there has been a bit of movement here.\n\nIn PD 3.1 version 1.4 of the spec, transmitting Revision is purely optional for cables. In PD 3.1 version 1.6, it is \"CN12/O/I\" with this note: \"Note 12: Shall be supported by Active Cables.\". So, responding to Get_Revision will be required by active cables going forward.\n\nWe should start seeing active cables support this, but until we have a feature where cable revision impacts functionality, I think this should be a lower priority.",
      "parentUuid": "877e203f_a7f0f502",
      "revId": "d9f970db98d333cc8e6bdacbbb4160daa0fec9c0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
